{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nnv1x3eCtyJy6SKkWgyogr","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review review form soundness novelty overall assessment score scale 1-5\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewform.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewform.md\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"}]\n\nI found information about the ACL Rolling Review form and scoring scales. Here's what the search results show:\n\n## Overall Assessment Score Scale\n\nThe overall assessment uses a scale that includes: 5 = Consider for Award (papers that could be considered for outstanding paper awards, up to top 2.5%); 2 = Resubmit next cycle (papers needing substantial revisions completable by next ARR cycle); 1.5 = Resubmit after next cycle (papers needing substantial revisions that cannot be completed by next cycle); and 1 = Do not resubmit (papers that need full redoing or are not relevant to ACL).\n\n## Scoring Components\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nThe overall assessment score is a composite score reflecting assessment of soundness, excitement, and other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n## Soundness and Novelty Assessment\n\nFor Findings papers, the main criteria are soundness and reproducibility, while conference recommendations may also consider novelty, impact and other factors.\n\nReviewers evaluate whether papers are sufficiently sound and thorough, whether they clearly state scientific claims and provide adequate support, and for experimental papers, they consider the depth and/or breadth of research questions investigated, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"806625a1-4285-4bea-b47f-2ce42ec65c53","uuid":"6064c2c3-7a7a-41be-ade4-22bacaed88e8","timestamp":"2026-05-16T10:06:10.854Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review review form soundness novelty overall assessment score scale 1-5","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014mDVgsbjrGf2k69CaxX2sE","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewform.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewform.md"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"}]},"I found information about the ACL Rolling Review form and scoring scales. Here's what the search results show:\n\n## Overall Assessment Score Scale\n\nThe overall assessment uses a scale that includes: 5 = Consider for Award (papers that could be considered for outstanding paper awards, up to top 2.5%); 2 = Resubmit next cycle (papers needing substantial revisions completable by next ARR cycle); 1.5 = Resubmit after next cycle (papers needing substantial revisions that cannot be completed by next cycle); and 1 = Do not resubmit (papers that need full redoing or are not relevant to ACL).\n\n## Scoring Components\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nThe overall assessment score is a composite score reflecting assessment of soundness, excitement, and other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n## Soundness and Novelty Assessment\n\nFor Findings papers, the main criteria are soundness and reproducibility, while conference recommendations may also consider novelty, impact and other factors.\n\nReviewers evaluate whether papers are sufficiently sound and thorough, whether they clearly state scientific claims and provide adequate support, and for experimental papers, they consider the depth and/or breadth of research questions investigated, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation."],"durationSeconds":6.655566121999996}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QBQJ68BukTn82aHCnghdZX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review 2026 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md\"}]\n\nI found detailed information about ACL Rolling Review 2026 reviewer guidelines, the review form, and scoring criteria. Here's what I found:\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines\n\nThe ARR peer review guidelines are a work-in-progress and will be updated as ARR evolves, and reviewers should check whether the version they are familiar with is still the current one before starting an assignment.\n\n## Scoring Criteria\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nThe scoring includes:\n\n- **Soundness**: If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\n- **Excitement**: Personal preferences should be reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper, and excitement scores reflect personal taste and do not necessarily come with explicit reasons.\n\n- **Overall Assessment**: The Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue.\n\n## Review Form Scoring\n\nFor the excitement score specifically, a score of 5 = Highly Exciting means \"I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference.\"\n\nFor overall recommendations, 5 = Consider for Award means \"I think this paper could be considered for an outstanding paper award at an *ACL conference (up to top 2.5% papers).\"\n\nYou can access the full reviewer guidelines at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines and the review form at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"806625a1-4285-4bea-b47f-2ce42ec65c53","uuid":"9936a63d-af73-40ab-8e4c-4dc501f52351","timestamp":"2026-05-16T10:06:11.906Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review 2026 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01NGXbnceDv65CR1exAKyvzs","content":[{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md"}]},"I found detailed information about ACL Rolling Review 2026 reviewer guidelines, the review form, and scoring criteria. Here's what I found:\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines\n\nThe ARR peer review guidelines are a work-in-progress and will be updated as ARR evolves, and reviewers should check whether the version they are familiar with is still the current one before starting an assignment.\n\n## Scoring Criteria\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nThe scoring includes:\n\n- **Soundness**: If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\n- **Excitement**: Personal preferences should be reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper, and excitement scores reflect personal taste and do not necessarily come with explicit reasons.\n\n- **Overall Assessment**: The Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue.\n\n## Review Form Scoring\n\nFor the excitement score specifically, a score of 5 = Highly Exciting means \"I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference.\"\n\nFor overall recommendations, 5 = Consider for Award means \"I think this paper could be considered for an outstanding paper award at an *ACL conference (up to top 2.5% papers).\"\n\nYou can access the full reviewer guidelines at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines and the review form at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform."],"durationSeconds":8.036822014000002}}
